# Local-only working material: never committed. Anchored to the repository root with a leading
# slash: an unanchored `.claude/` matches at any depth, and it silently swallowed the fixture
# trees under core/tests/fixtures — which look fine locally, because the files are on disk, and
# arrive in CI as cases with no input at all.
/internal/
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/
# wayfinder maps and decision tickets: planning, not product
/.scratch/

# Rust
/target/

.DS_Store
.build/
.swiftpm/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
build/
# Build output, not source. The app's `dist/` holds its checked-in frontend — a static index
# today — so the rule stays unanchored everywhere except where source lives.
/dist/
/internal/prototype/dist/
*.dmg
*.p12
*.cer
*.mobileprovision
secrets/
